<title>ESTONIA: BALTIKA TO MERGE TWO RETAIL SUBSIDIARIES.</title>
<headline>BALTIKA TO MERGE TWO RETAIL SUBSIDIARIES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baltika said on Wednesday that in the second quarter of 1997 it will merge its two largest retail subsidiaries, Baltman and Baltika Kaubandusgrup.</p>
<p>In a statement, the clothing and retail firm said that the merged company will trade under the name of Baltman and it expects retail trade of 50 million kroons in Estonia in 1997.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
